You track combat state in a Pathfinder 1e adventure. Emit ONLY the
deltas the engine should apply on top of the existing combat context.
Never restate identity (`name`, `type`, `max_hp`, `armor_class`).

=== WHAT HAPPENED ===
<%= @what_happened %>

=== MUTATIONS APPLIED ===
<%= @mutations_json.present? ? @mutations_json : "(no mechanical mutations)" %>

<% if @canonical_hp.present? -%>
=== CANONICAL HP (current HP after mutations) ===
<%= @canonical_hp %>
<% end -%>

<% if @canonical_participants.present? -%>
=== CURRENT PARTICIPANTS (the only actor_sheet_id values you may reference) ===
<%= @canonical_participants.to_json %>
<% end -%>

=== CURRENT COMBAT CONTEXT ===
<%= @current_context.present? ? @current_context.to_json : "(empty)" %>

=== INSTRUCTIONS ===
- `participant_updates` is a delta channel for HP / condition changes
  the narrative produced that MUTATIONS APPLIED did not already cover.
  Each entry references an `actor_sheet_id` from CURRENT PARTICIPANTS
  (integer); never invent ids; never include the player.
- `hp_delta` is the integer change to apply on top of CANONICAL HP.
  Negative for damage, positive for healing. Engine clamps to
  `[0, max_hp]`.
- `conditions_added` / `conditions_removed` are short string arrays
  (e.g. `"prone"`, `"frightened"`).
- `round` and `turn_order` are top-level. Emit only when the narrative
  itself advanced the round or reordered initiative.
- `active: false` ends the encounter when every hostile NPC is
  eliminated or the situation defuses (surrender, parley, flight).
  The engine never licenses you to set `active: true` — combat starts
  via the `combat_initialization` mutation, not this step.

Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences). Omit any
key you don't need; an empty `{}` means no change.

Example — incidental damage from a narrative event:
{
  "participant_updates": [
    { "actor_sheet_id": 273, "hp_delta": -3, "conditions_added": ["prone"] }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Lord Velkar slipped on the wet stone for 3 bludgeoning and went prone."
}

Example — combat ended by narrative resolution:
{
  "active": false,
  "reasoning": "All hostiles surrendered after the captain yielded."
}

Example — nothing relevant happened:
{}
